think The fixed 1,024-round road is complete (GRAD sealed); the bench climbs the double-seat expansion. REMEMBER's live edge + the last session log named the next Lindy-first crux plainly: Cord r2 — Byzantine refusal. The design read (20260813-032851) fixed r2 as equivocation refusal onto r1's spine known correct.
think The adversary a leaderless DAG must survive is equivocation — one author publishing two distinct blocks at the same round, hoping honest nodes admit different ones and split history. r1's add refuses BadSignature · DanglingParent · TooManyParents · DagFull · Duplicate, but two DISTINCT blocks from one author at one round (different hashes) would both admit. r2 closes that.
think Kept it additive per the reviving/finishing discipline: r1's add stays a green binary, r2 is its own file mycelium/cord_byzantine.rye composing r1 public API. Grew two small additive pubs on cord.rye — address (a block's SHA-256, to tell a Duplicate at the same hash from an Equivocation at a different hash) and verify_block (the signature check, extracted so add and add_bft share one crypto check rather than duplicate it). r1 selftest re-ran GREEN after the refactor.
think add_bft's order is load-bearing and truthful: reject a forgery (BadSignature) BEFORE classifying an equivocation, so a garbage block carrying a real author's key-bytes cannot pose as one; then is_equivocation (same author + same round + different address among held blocks); then delegate to r1 add. is_equivocation skips the same-round-different-author and the same-block (equal address, a Duplicate for r1) cases honestly.
think The r2 crux proven on metal: build the honest four-block Dag, record its committed order and fold state; attempt author A's second distinct genesis at round 0 (validly signed by A, fact 999 memo genesis-a-evil) — refused Equivocation, dag len unchanged; commit again — byte-identical order, identical fold state (issued 1000 · taxed 300 · supply 700 · one star). The equivocator gains zero ordering weight. Four supporting cases: same author at a LATER round admitted (per-round not per-author); a forward reference refuses DanglingParent (so a block points only backward — no cycle can form); a forgery refuses BadSignature not Equivocation.
obs The n/3 Byzantine-threshold framing in the design is honored here as a mechanism, not an over-claim: safety is by admission control (at most one block per author per round), so an equivocator never outweighs an honest author. A simulated f<n/3 fault-tolerance benchmark stays a named later round; the witness proves what it runs (Two Rooms).
